5. ONE INTERMITTENT BUILD FAILURE, OBSERVED ONCE AND NOT REPRODUCED
===============================================================================

Recorded because a gate that only reports its successful runs is not a gate.

The FIRST clean-clone attempt at edc4054 failed the build with two errors:

  error MSB3030: Could not copy the file
  "...\src\Merchandising.Inventory\bin\Debug\net10.0-windows\
   Merchandising.Inventory.runtimeconfig.json" because it was not found.
  [...\src\tests\Merchandising.Tests.Unit\Merchandising.Tests.Unit.vbproj]

  (and the same for Merchandising.Procurement.runtimeconfig.json)

This is not a compile error and names no source file. Merchandising.Tests.Unit
references two OutputType=WinExe projects - Inventory (since P1-15) and
Procurement (since P3-07) - and in a parallel build the referenced
executable's runtimeconfig.json can be listed as a copy-local item before the
task that generates it has run.

ATTRIBUTION, measured rather than assumed. Nine clean-clone builds were run:

  commit    full runs (build + both suites)   build-only runs   MSB3030
  -------   ------------------------------    ---------------   -------
  edc4054   2                                 3                 1 of 5
  7480c43   2                                 3                 0 of 4

It appeared once, on the first run at edc4054, and never again on either
commit. The project references that cause it BOTH predate this gate - the
Procurement reference is in the vbproj that shipped with P3-07's original
commit, not added here - so this is a pre-existing fragility that one run
happened to expose, not a regression introduced by closing P3-07. Four out
of four later runs at edc4054 were clean, including the two full runs whose
output is quoted above.

NOT claimed: that it is fixed, or that the true rate is 1 in 9. It was seen
once and has not been reproduced, and nine runs is too small a sample to put
a number on it. It is left recorded rather than repaired because the repair
belongs to whoever owns build infrastructure, not to P3-07, and because the
condition it threatens - a classmate's first build from a clean clone
(ADR-012) - is retried by simply building again. Worth a card if it recurs.
